$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: EXPERIMENTAL A mixture of the carbonyl
compound (5, 1.0mmol), arylhydrazine (6, 1.2mmol), and the solid acid (7,
Amberlite, 1.5g, obtained from Aldrich Chemical Co.) was refluxed in
absolute ethanol (10ml) for 8h. The reaction was monitored by thin-layer
chromatography (TLC), and upon completion the mixture was cooled to room
temperature, the catalyst filtered off, and and the product was washed
thoroughly with ethyl acetate (30ml). The combined organics were washed
with water, dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting
residue was chromatographed on a silica gel column eluting with ethyl
acetate-hexane mixtures. The purified indole (8). This was fully
characterized by infrared, 400-MHz 1H NMR, high-resolution mass
spectrometry, and melting point (solids). 4 3-Isopropyl-1-H-indole.
purified on silica gel 100-200 mesh (EtOAc/Hexane 10/90); yellowish
solid, yield 70%. TLC Rf 0.35 (20% EtOAc/Hexane); mp 38-40°C (lit.1
40-42°C); ν max 3872, 2956, 1450, 1124; δH 7.81-7.79 (m, 2H), 7.39-7.37
(d, 1H, J 8 Hz), 7.33-7.31 (d, 1H, J 8 Hz), 7.27-7.23 (t, 1H, J 6.8 Hz),
6.97-6.96 (d, 1H, J 4 Hz), 3.37-3.30 (m, 1H), 1.50-1.48 (d, 6H, J 8 Hz);
δH 136.5, 126.7, 123.8, 121.7, 119.3, 118.9, 111.1, 25.4, 23.2; m/z
calcd. for M+H 160.1024, found 160.1029.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, Amberlite IR 120 resin in H+ form used, Fischer
indole synthesis, reusable catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A convenient modification of the Fischer indole synthesis with a solid
acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chandrasekhar, Sosale; Mukherjee, Somnath
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2015), 45(8), 1018-1022

